[Adapter]
; Read once at game start unless a line says otherwise. Without Enabled=1 the add-on
; keeps its earlier behaviour (mirroring the game's own Vulkan DLSS).
Enabled=0
; Source=fg-input runs Generic's Present layers on the real frame at the native
; frame-generation input (before DLSS-G interpolates).
;Source=fg-input
; Follow=1 runs NR continuously whenever Generic selects this path: a non-zero Present
;  layer count with a stage-protocol Generic (DLSS5StageProtocolVersion()==1), or
;  NRHookPoint=Present with an older Generic. Without Follow=1 (or AutoRun=1) NR runs
;  only for development request files.
;Follow=1
; Pipeline=2 (default) is the GPU relay: the input copies become this add-on's own
;  Vulkan batch on DLSSG.CmdQueue and the FG evaluate's park is released from the GPU
;  as soon as the private D3D12 NR is done. 3 copies at the game's vkQueuePresentKHR
;  instead (about 5 ms earlier). 0 is the serial feed, for diagnosis only: it parks the
;  FG evaluate on the CPU for the whole NR, so the generated frames reach the screen in
;  bursts (a high frame counter with uneven display); the log warns when it is set.
;  1 runs the same NR concurrently and discards it (throughput probe; picture carries no NR).
;Pipeline=2
; SerialFallback=1 lets the serial feed take over when the relay stands down. By default
;  NR at the FG input pauses instead, the private session is rebuilt and the relay is
;  retried, up to 3 times per process.
;SerialFallback=0
; Import=1 (default) releases the park on the GPU through a D3D12 fence imported as a
;  Vulkan timeline semaphore, and adds VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32 to the game's
;  device at creation (a hook on the ReShade layer's vkCreateDevice that appends the
;  name to a copy of the create info; a driver that refuses the name gets the caller's
;  own list retried unchanged, so device creation cannot fail because of it). The import
;  is used only for a device that accepted the name. Import=0 keeps a CPU gate that left
;  a quarter to half of the frames without NR in the game, and disables the throttle.
;Import=1
; Throttle=N (default 1, 0 off, at most 3; needs Import=1) holds the game at the top of
;  its frame (after slReflexSleep, before input and simulation) until the NR of the
;  newest queued frame, less N-1 frames, has completed; a game that never calls
;  slReflexSleep is held at its vkQueuePresentKHR instead. Reflex cannot see the NR on
;  the private D3D12 queue, so without this a GPU-bound game runs ahead and frames queue
;  in front of the NR, which shows as input latency. Each wait is bounded to 250 ms;
;  five timeouts in a row stand the throttle down for 5 s, then it re-arms itself.
;Throttle=1
; Trace=1 adds pass-through observers (game present, slSetTag, queue submits, FG
;  handles, FG command-buffer submits) to the log. Asynchronous bounded logging; no
;  rendering parameter changes.
;Trace=0
; FocusKeepFG=1 (default) keeps DLSS-G running while the game window is visible but not
;  focused, when NR runs at the FG input and Streamline's focus check can be identified
;  (Streamline 2.14.1; the 2.10.3 files Endfield ships keep their own behaviour).
;FocusKeepFG=1
; HoldComposition=1 (default) keeps DWM composing the game's monitor while NR runs at the
;  FG input and the game window is shown: a 2x2, near-transparent, click-through,
;  non-activating tool window of this process sits at that monitor's top-left corner.
;  Without it, Windows promotes the unfocused game to Independent Flip and back, and
;  Streamline presents ~12 raw frames without FG (hence without NR) at each switch.
;  Read every second; 0 removes it.
;HoldComposition=1
; HoldCompositionAlpha=1..255 (default 1) is that window's opacity. Read every second.
;HoldCompositionAlpha=1
; HoldCompositionHideCapture=1 excludes that window from screenshots and recordings.
;  Off by default: with it, the NVIDIA overlay refused to take screenshots of the game.
;  Read every second.
;HoldCompositionHideCapture=0
